#: ../../mayavi/docs/source/mayavi/auto/example_volume_slicer.rst:8
#: ../../mayavi/docs/source/mayavi/auto/examples.rst:494
msgid ""
"Example of an elaborate dialog showing a multiple views on the same data, "
"with 3 cuts synchronized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../mayavi/docs/source/mayavi/auto/example_volume_slicer.rst:11
msgid ""
"This example shows how to have multiple views on the same data, how to "
"embedded multiple scenes in a dialog, and the caveat in populating them with"
" data, as well as how to add some interaction logic on an ImagePlaneWidget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../mayavi/docs/source/mayavi/auto/example_volume_slicer.rst:16
msgid ""
"The order in which things happen in this example is important, and it is "
"easy to get it wrong. First of all, many properties of the visualization "
"objects cannot be changed if there is not a scene created to view them. This"
" is why we put a lot of the visualization logic in the callback of "
"scene.activated, which is called after creation of the scene. Second, "
"default values created via the '_xxx_default' callback are created lazily, "
"that is, when the attributes are accessed. As the establishment of the VTK "
"pipeline can depend on the order in which it is built, we trigger these "
"access by explicitly calling the attributes. In particular, properties like "
"scene background color, or interaction properties cannot be set before the "
"scene is activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../mayavi/docs/source/mayavi/auto/example_volume_slicer.rst:28
msgid ""
"The same data is exposed in the different scenes by sharing the VTK dataset "
"between different Mayavi data sources. See the "
":ref:`sharing_data_between_scenes` tip for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../mayavi/docs/source/mayavi/auto/example_volume_slicer.rst:32
msgid ""
"In this example, the interaction with the scene and the various elements on "
"it is strongly simplified by turning off interaction, and choosing specific "
"scene interactor styles. Indeed, non-technical users can be confused with "
"too rich interaction."
msgstr ""

